  "step_3": "The information relevant to the decision reason — comparing the most probable outcomes (4000€ at 80% vs. 3000€ at 100%) — is not explicitly mentioned or evaluated in the verbal report. The individual does not refer to the most probable outcome of either lottery, nor does the individual state that they preferred the lottery with the more favorable most probable outcome. Instead, the justification is based on the perceived sufficiency of 3000 euros and the unwillingness to accept a lower probability (i.e., risk), which reflects a different decision rationale (e.g., risk aversion or utility-based preference). Therefore, the individual did not use the decision reason that focuses on the most probable outcome. The comparison of the most probable outcomes is missing, and the justification does not follow the rule of the decision reason. Thus, the decision reason was not used.",
  "final_assessment_score": 0
